From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:47:07 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 099/230] Give the timeline, club page, live cards and shot
 grid a visual pass
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Match detail's timeline is a rail now: one marker per event, tinted with the
club that caused it and carrying that event's own mark (ball, card, swap).
The marks are drawn, not emoji — a colour emoji ignores currentColor, renders
differently on every platform and breaks the one-meaning-per-colour rule — so
a booking reads gold, a sending-off danger and a goal volt.

The club page opens on the club's own colour washing out of one corner into
the surface, with the crest at a new 64px hero size.

A live match card wears a cyan halo plus a slow ring pulse (opacity only), so
live separates from scheduled and finished cards at a glance.

Shot Plotter reads as a pitch: a turf plate under white markings — goal line,
penalty area, six-yard box, halfway line, centre circle — with a selected zone
lifting 6% and filling with a volt wash.

